{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.PerNeutronLadder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.PerNeutronLadder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Hom.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.PerNeutronLadder.parity_ladders_arithmetic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.PerNeutronLadder.parity_ladders_arithmetic","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/PerNeutronLadder.lean#L74-L87","doc":"**Parity descent of arithmetic ladders.** If the `q₀`-leg and the\n`q₀⁻¹`-leg are both arithmetic (steps `ℓ`, `ℓ'`), the bar-even\ncombination `L + L'` and the bar-odd combination `L − L'` are\narithmetic with steps `ℓ + ℓ'` and `ℓ − ℓ'` — hence each satisfies\nthe same degenerate `c = 2` recurrence. The archimedean instance is\nthe probe's per-neutron parity quanta `E₀·ℓ_even`, `E₀·ℓ_odd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.PerNeutronLadder.two_sigma_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.PerNeutronLadder.two_sigma_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/PerNeutronLadder.lean#L66-L72","doc":"**The degenerate multiplier is σ-fixed for every ring hom.** So the\nhypothesis of `QOU.Knot.SelfDuality.recurrence_descent` holds with\n`c = 2` for ANY bar-involution — which is exactly why the probe's\nparity tie at `c = 2` is real but carries no non-trivial\nAskey–Wilson content: every arithmetic ladder ties its parities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.PerNeutronLadder.arithmetic_degenerate_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.PerNeutronLadder.arithmetic_degenerate_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/PerNeutronLadder.lean#L55-L64","doc":"**Arithmetic ladder ⇒ degenerate three-term recurrence.** A\nconstant-step ladder (the log-leg of a geometric one) satisfies\n`V₊ = c·Vₖ − V₋` with the degenerate multiplier `c = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.PerNeutronLadder.geometric_multiplicative_casoratian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.PerNeutronLadder.geometric_multiplicative_casoratian","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/PerNeutronLadder.lean#L43-L53","doc":"**Geometric ⇒ vanishing multiplicative Casoratian.** The\nmultiplicative avatar of the degenerate `c = 2` recurrence — the\nprobe's exact finding about the free/atom trace ratio, stated\nwithout any `log` (generic `R`, §7c). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.PerNeutronLadder.geometric_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.PerNeutronLadder.geometric_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/PerNeutronLadder.lean#L34-L41","doc":"**Geometric ladder ⇒ closed form.** If each neutron multiplies the\ntrace ratio by a fixed `ρ`, the ladder is `ρ^n`-geometric. ","signatureChunk":0}]}